From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 15:08:15 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 133/139] phy: qcom: qmp-combo: Leave the USB PCS alone in
 DP-only mode

In DP-only mode (pin assignments C and E) the four lanes belong to the
DisplayPort PHY and the mux switch has already powered the USB PCS
down. The USB controller can still init and exit its PHY in this state,
e.g. across a system suspend that loses power: qmp_combo_usb_init()
then programs the USB serdes tables over the DP configuration and times
out waiting for PHYSTATUS, and qmp_combo_usb_exit() decrements
usb_init_count a second time.

Only take and drop the common reference in DP-only mode. The USB PCS is
powered up by the mux switch when the port leaves DP-only mode.

On a Lenovo TB323FU (Kaanapali) with a USB-C monitor in pin assignment
C, resume from s2idle failed with "phy initialization timed-out", the
dwc3 resume returned -110 and the following xHCI resume hung the
system.

Signed-off-by: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
index 7381d7483..28be336ab 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -4341,6 +4341,9 @@ static int qmp_combo_usb_init(struct phy *phy)
 	if (ret)
 		goto out_unlock;
 
+	if (qmp->qmpphy_mode == QMPPHY_MODE_DP_ONLY)
+		goto out_unlock;
+
 	ret = qmp_combo_usb_power_on(phy);
 	if (ret) {
 		qmp_combo_com_exit(qmp, false);
@@ -4360,6 +4363,11 @@ static int qmp_combo_usb_exit(struct phy *phy)
 	int ret;
 
 	mutex_lock(&qmp->phy_mutex);
+	if (qmp->qmpphy_mode == QMPPHY_MODE_DP_ONLY) {
+		ret = qmp_combo_com_exit(qmp, false);
+		goto out_unlock;
+	}
+
 	ret = qmp_combo_usb_power_off(phy);
 	if (ret)
 		goto out_unlock;
